! GeoView, views to display and interact with geographical objects and cartographic layers
 
Pierre LABORDE (pierre.laborde@fr.thalesgroup.com)
Eric LE PORS (eric.lepors@fr.thalesgroup.com)
Paul BLOTTIERE (paul.blottiere@hytech-imaging.fr)

""Abstract:""
GeoView is a geographic display library written for Pharo. GeoView enables the creation and management of the display of geo-referenced objects, as a geographic information systems (GIS). The library offers view composition with specialized display layers and projection functions. A cartographic layer compatible with the best standards is provided to display map backgrounds. This cartographic layer integrates the WMS and WMTS standards and connects to any compatible server. GeoView offers an implementation for Block via the Alexandrie backend (for good performance) and is designed to be portable to other display technologies if needed.

""Bio:""
Pierre LABORDE and Eric LE PORS are working at Thales in Brest, France. They are User Experience and Software engineer specialized in defense domains. Paul Blottiere is a QGIS contributor and FOSS enthusiast.
